							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;"><div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=3342.msg37520#msg37520">Quote from: namski on September 26, 2007, 12:15:02 am</a></div><div class="quote"><div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=3342.msg37519#msg37519">Quote from: virtuousvandal on September 26, 2007, 12:05:25 am</a></div><div class="quote"><br />I&#039;m not personally a fan of The Game, but I have heard at least one of his songs that I think had redeeming value<br />the point that I&#039;m trying to make is what about when there is no redeeming&nbsp; value aside from plain lyrical skill in any of an individuals songs, when it&#039;s all about livin it up in the scar face fantasy minus that part at the end when he gets shot up.<br />I mean not all music has a specific message, but with Rick Ross I do hear a message that&#039;s saying &quot;I don&#039;t care how many lives coke fucks up. as long as I&#039;m rich and powerful and I got plenty of tang, I&#039;m happy.&quot;<br /><br />by the way, can someone please explain to me the term &quot;backpacker music&quot; and where the hell it came from<br /></div><br />yeah...i dont listen to Rick Ross...but im sure you&#039;re not exaggerating about his content. Artists know that they make money off that kinda rap...they know, cuz obviously their audiences wanna hear it. Those who listen to it, sometimes dont realize what they&#039;re listening to....and if they do realize it and like it enough to support the music, well...then there&#039;s a problem. Then the artists get comfortable. We&#039;ll see how far do some rappers go, in the future.<br /><br />the rap music that is gettin hella play and airtime is getting more and more dumbed down. <br /></div><br />for real<br />so the reason this stuff gets play isn&#039;t because it should, but because it can.<br />maybe I should have had this in the &quot;By any Means Category.&quot;</div>
